# A typed copy of a loop reads its list through the storage that was read in front of its turns. As users build no turn asks whether the list has changed: everything hangs on the turn LEAVING for the closed copy BEFORE an operation that may move the storage, and on what the turns do being heard.
# THE LIE, testing=TypedTurnsPassStoresIntoListsOver: the turn of a typed copy does not leave at a store into a list, and the tries do not hear the store; the store itself is made and ends what it writes.
# The function of filter appends eight elements to its own source, which moves the source's storage, and then stores ahead: under the lie alone filter goes on reading the old storage and misses what was stored: a wrong answer in silence.
# Under --aot-harden=ignore-told-ranges (testing=TestsEveryPosition) and under proof-checks (testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime) the emitter holds the storage against a fresh read off the list in every turn: the process stops by name.
# The second function stores ahead and moves nothing: it is right under the lie too.
